--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- POLYESTER mooring with DYNAMIC axial stiffness (viscoelastic, ElasticMod 2)
-- A synthetic-rope mooring's stiffness is NOT a single EA: it is lower under a slow mean load
-- (the static stiffness Es) and higher under wave-frequency cycling (the dynamic stiffness Ed).
-- CableDyn represents this with the two-branch series-Kelvin model of MoorDyn ElasticMod 2 (a
-- standard linear solid only when the dynamic-branch dashpot Bd is zero): the EA column is
-- bar-separated `Es|Ed`, and the BA column is the matching `Bs|Bd` dashpot constants (N-s, both
-- non-negative -- NOT the -zeta convention that EI=0 chain lines use). The static IC solves with
-- Es; a dynamic run engages the Ed branch. Properties are the md_viscoelastic r-test polyester
-- rope (Es 1.424e8, Ed 2.5e8, Bs 4.0e9, Bd 1.1e7, 22.42 kg/m, 0.1438 m) on the Lozon Gulf of
-- Maine 200 m geometry -- a grounded semi-taut catenary that converges robustly.
